Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] NTCamera: offer 4K60 on Galaxian

ConfigMapGalaxian (chosen from ro.product.device=Galaxian) seeds
FeatureConfigParser.sConfigMap with

    FEATURE_CAMERA_4K_60FPS_SUPPORT -> v3   # the shared "false" scratch
    FEATURE_CAMERA_SUPER_NIGHT      -> v2   # the shared "true" scratch

so the app never offers 4K60 even though the pipeline accepts 60fps.
Point that single put at v2, the register already holding "true".

This mirrors what the Tetris port (NtCam_Port v1.23) does to
ConfigMapGalaxian in its dex patch, where it appends a second put of the
same key with "true" after the stock one instead of editing the shared
register.

Whether the vendor pipeline really accepts 4K + 60fps for a given
camera/mode is still up to the HAL; the app only exposes the choice.

---
--- a/smali_classes5/com/nothing/common/utils/config/ConfigMapGalaxian.smali
+++ b/smali_classes5/com/nothing/common/utils/config/ConfigMapGalaxian.smali
@@ -407,7 +407,7 @@
 
     const-string v1, "FEATURE_CAMERA_4K_60FPS_SUPPORT"
 
-    invoke-virtual {v0, v1, v3}, Ljava/util/HashMap;->put(Ljava/lang/Object;Ljava/lang/Object;)Ljava/lang/Object;
+    invoke-virtual {v0, v1, v2}, Ljava/util/HashMap;->put(Ljava/lang/Object;Ljava/lang/Object;)Ljava/lang/Object;
 
     .line 66
     sget-object v0, Lcom/nothing/common/utils/FeatureConfigParser;->sConfigMap:Ljava/util/HashMap;
